#undef NDEBUG
// Review HE: Declare keyed by a typed attribute on an XES upload's log
// shape, the activity set pm4py's Declare discovery iterates, and the
// Inductive miner keyed by a column with no value.
//
// - On an XES upload's log shape (read_xes' legacy log), Declare keyed by an
//   attribute of ints (past int64 too), floats, booleans, dates or valueless
//   values keys its rules frame by the objects the importer stores (a date
//   in UTC with its wall clock kept, an absent key a KeyError, a list with
//   children unhashable), so the TypeErrors, KeyErrors and models follow
//   the DataFrame shape's typed model.
// - pm4py iterates a copy of the activity set (set(set(...))), whose table
//   is sized afresh from five activities on: the rules frame's columns and
//   the auto threshold's sort follow the copy's order (the operand order of
//   its TypeError), on CSV and XES uploads alike; a date column with a gap
//   hashes NaT as -2**63.
// - The Inductive miner keyed by a column of gaps only (read_csv's float64
//   NaN) raises pandas' errors (one event: __str__ returned non-string, one
//   event per case: maximum recursion depth, else can only concatenate str)
//   or, on Polars, a tau tree for one event per case and otherwise None
//   cannot be a node.
//
// Expected values are pm4py 2.7.22 black-box on the same inputs
// (review-harness round-he: tc/mkhe.py, ct/dcx.py, p/igs.py).
//
// Usage: minera_server_review_he_tests <minera_server>
